IMPORT prelude

-- Home Affairs Uniformed Services Superannuation Act 2001 (Singapore) -- who the INVEST Plan covers (ss 2, 3(1), 4(1)), who may
-- dismiss a member and who may cut a benefit (s 6), what a creditor may take (s 7), bankruptcy and imprisonment (ss 8, 9), recovery
-- of a benefit wrongly granted (s 11), the Board's investment bar and constitution (ss 15, 19), appeals against awards (s 23) and
-- the Fund's financial year (s 24(9)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HAUSSA2001.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and came into operation on 31 December 2021; the latest amendment annotated in
-- the body is Act 35 of 2019 (the Legislative History lists Act 40 of 2018, in force 30 July 2020, last). SSO marked it the
-- "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026" when retrieved.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0173 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person it applies to -- here, a police, civil defence,
-- narcotics, prison or intelligence officer and his or her family; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The benefits themselves: the Act leaves the INVEST Plan, its contributions, rates and retirement ages to regulations
-- (s 3(2), (3)), none of which were retrieved, so no amount is computed here. Also not encoded: s 4(2) (the value guaranteed to
-- converting officers), s 5 (no absolute right), s 6(2) beyond who decides, s 8(4) and s 9(3) (the Minister's discretion to pay the
-- family), s 10 (death benefits held on trust), the Fund's receipts and purposes (ss 12-14, 16-18), Board functions and delegation
-- (ss 20-22), audit (s 24(1)-(8)), periodic examination (s 25) and regulations (s 26).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Home Affairs Uniformed Services Superannuation Act 2001 -- the INVEST Plan`

DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `a civil defence officer`
    `an intelligence officer`
    `a narcotics officer`
    `a junior police officer`
    `a senior police officer`
    `a prison officer`
    `an auxiliary police officer`
    `a Special Constabulary member`
    `a police national serviceman`

§§ `2 -- uniformed service officer`

-- s 2: "police officer" means a public officer appointed to the permanent establishment in the Police Service "but excludes any
-- auxiliary police officer, any member of the Special Constabulary ... and any police officer who is a national serviceman";
-- "junior police officer" is one "below the rank of inspector"; "uniformed service officer" means "any civil defence officer,
-- intelligence officer, narcotics officer, police officer or prison officer".
GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a uniformed service officer` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `an auxiliary police officer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Special Constabulary member` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a police national serviceman` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `serves in one of the four Services named in s 4(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `a civil defence officer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a narcotics officer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a junior police officer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a senior police officer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a prison officer` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3(1), 4(1) -- coming into the INVEST Plan`

-- s 3(1): the Plan is for civil defence, narcotics, police and prison officers "appointed on or after the commencement of the
-- regulations", and intelligence officers so appointed.
-- s 4(1): an officer of those four Services (NOT intelligence officers) appointed before the commencement who is then (a) eligible
-- for a pension, gratuity or allowance under the Pensions Act 1956, or (b) on a contract and eligible for a gratuity under it, is
-- given "an option to join the INVEST Plan".
-- s 4(1)(b) speaks of "every officer" appointed to those Services on a contract; whether such an officer is a "uniformed service
-- officer" (permanent establishment) the text does not say. This encoding treats the four-Service kinds as covering both (an
-- inference).
DECLARE Entry IS ONE OF
    `a member on appointment`
    `offered an option to join`
    `not brought in by the Act`

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
      `appointed on or after the regulations began` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligible under the Pensions Act just before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligible for a contract gratuity just before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entry
DECIDE `how the officer comes into the INVEST Plan` IS
    IF NOT `is a uniformed service officer` `the officer` THEN `not brought in by the Act`
    ELSE IF `appointed on or after the regulations began` THEN `a member on appointment`
         ELSE IF `serves in one of the four Services named in s 4(1)` `the officer`
                 AND (`eligible under the Pensions Act just before` OR `eligible for a contract gratuity just before`)
              THEN `offered an option to join`
              ELSE `not brought in by the Act`

§§ `6(1), (3), (4) -- who may dismiss, who may cut a benefit`

-- s 6(1): nothing in the Act "limits the right of the relevant appointing authority to dismiss any member ... without compensation".
-- (2): on "negligence, irregularity or misconduct" the relevant authority may "reduce or altogether withhold" the benefit (subject
-- to Article 113 of the Constitution).
-- (3): appointing authority -- junior police officer: the Commissioner of Police; others: the Public Service Commission or its
-- delegates. (4): relevant authority -- junior police officer: the Commissioner of Police; others: a Permanent Secretary to the
-- Ministry of Home Affairs or delegates.
DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner of Police`
    `the Public Service Commission or a delegate`
    `a Permanent Secretary of Home Affairs or a delegate`
    `none named, not a member`

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH AN Authority
DECIDE `who may dismiss the member` IS
    IF NOT `is a uniformed service officer` `the officer` THEN `none named, not a member`
    ELSE IF `the officer` EQUALS `a junior police officer` THEN `the Commissioner of Police`
         ELSE `the Public Service Commission or a delegate`

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH AN Authority
DECIDE `who may reduce or withhold the benefit` IS
    IF NOT `is a uniformed service officer` `the officer` THEN `none named, not a member`
    ELSE IF `the officer` EQUALS `a junior police officer` THEN `the Commissioner of Police`
         ELSE `a Permanent Secretary of Home Affairs or a delegate`

§§ `7 -- what a creditor may take`

-- s 7: no benefit, Government contribution or interest is "assignable or transferable, or liable to be garnished, attached,
-- sequestered or levied upon for or in respect of any debt or claim, other than -- (a) a debt due to the Government; or (b) an order
-- of court for the payment of periodical sums of money towards the maintenance of the wife or former wife or minor child (whether
-- legitimate or not) of the member".
-- Read literally, a husband's maintenance order and a lump-sum order are not within (b).
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a debt due to the Government`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a wife`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a former wife`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a minor child born outside marriage`
    `a periodical maintenance order for an adult child`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a husband`
    `a lump-sum maintenance order for a wife`
    `a bank's judgment debt`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the benefit may be attached for the claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a periodical maintenance order for a wife` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a periodical maintenance order for a former wife` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a periodical maintenance order for a minor child born outside marriage` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `8, 9 -- bankruptcy and imprisonment`

-- s 8(2): if at retirement or resignation a member "has been adjudged a bankrupt ... and he or she has not obtained a discharge",
-- an award officer may "refuse to grant any pension, gratuity or other allowance".
GIVEN `adjudged bankrupt at retirement` IS A BOOLEAN, `discharged by then` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the award officer may refuse the award` IF
    `adjudged bankrupt at retirement` AND (NOT `discharged by then`)

-- s 8(3): a pensioner "adjudicated a bankrupt" -- the Minister "may direct that the pension or allowance must forthwith cease".
-- s 9(1): a pensioner "sentenced to death or penal servitude or any term of imprisonment by any court ... whether in Singapore or
-- elsewhere, for any crime or offence" -- likewise. A fine is not a sentence of imprisonment.
DECLARE Event IS ONE OF
    `adjudicated bankrupt`
    `sentenced to a term of imprisonment`
    `sentenced to imprisonment abroad`
    `sentenced to death`
    `fined only`

GIVEN `the event` IS AN Event
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may stop the pension` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `fined only` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 8(5): on "a full and proper discharge" from bankruptcy the pension "must be restored ... with effect from the date of the
-- discharge" -- so the months it was stopped are not repaid.
-- s 9(2): a pension stopped on conviction "must be restored with retrospective effect" on "a free pardon".
-- Serving the sentence restores nothing; s 9(3) only lets the Minister pay the family, or the pensioner after the sentence, at
-- discretion.
DECLARE Ending IS ONE OF
    `discharged from bankruptcy`
    `granted a free pardon`
    `released after serving the sentence`

GIVEN `the ending` IS AN Ending
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pension must be restored` IF
    CONSIDER `the ending`
    WHEN `released after serving the sentence` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the ending` IS AN Ending, `months the pension was stopped` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the stopped months that must be repaid` IS
    CONSIDER `the ending`
    WHEN `granted a free pardon` THEN `months the pension was stopped`
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `11 -- recovery of a benefit wrongly granted`

-- s 11: the Government "may recover, cancel or reduce the grant if it is shown to have been obtained by the wilful suppression of
-- material facts or to have been granted in ignorance of facts which, had they been known before the retirement or resignation of
-- the member, would have justified his or her dismissal or a reduction of his or her salary".
GIVEN `obtained by wilful suppression of material facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `granted in ignorance of facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those facts would have justified dismissal or a salary cut` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government may recover the grant` IF
        `obtained by wilful suppression of material facts`
    OR  (`granted in ignorance of facts` AND `those facts would have justified dismissal or a salary cut`)

§§ `15, 19 -- the Board`

-- s 15(1): the Board may invest "in such stocks, funds, securities and investments as the Board thinks fit (but not any stock, bond
-- or security issued by the Government)"; (4) "investments" include "the use of financial products (including ... any derivatives
-- contract) ... for the purposes of effective management of an investment portfolio".
DECLARE Investment IS ONE OF
    `Singapore Government securities`
    `listed shares`
    `corporate bonds`
    `derivatives used to manage the portfolio`

GIVEN `the investment` IS AN Investment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may invest in it` IF
    CONSIDER `the investment`
    WHEN `Singapore Government securities` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 19(1): "not less than 5 and not more than 15 persons"; (2) appointed for a period "not exceeding 3 years", eligible for
-- re-appointment.
GIVEN `trustees` IS A NUMBER, `term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board appointment is within s 19` IF
        `trustees` AT LEAST 5
    AND `trustees` AT MOST 15
    AND `term in years` AT MOST 3

§§ `23 -- appeals against awards`

-- s 23(2): "except as otherwise provided by any regulations ... no award of benefits under the INVEST Plan is subject to appeal to
-- any court". (3): the Minister or an appointee may review an award on appeal, "whether by increasing or decreasing the award", and
-- that decision "is final and conclusive and is not subject to appeal to any court".
-- (4): every appeal "must be brought within 12 months of the date the appellant is notified" of the award officer's decision, "or
-- such longer period as the Minister or person appointed ... may allow". Counting in whole months, 12 is treated as in time (an
-- inference on "within").
GIVEN `months since notified` IS A NUMBER, `a longer period allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `months since notified` AT MOST 12 OR `a longer period allowed`

GIVEN `it is the Minister's decision on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN, `regulations provide a court appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court may hear an appeal` IF
    (NOT `it is the Minister's decision on appeal`) AND `regulations provide a court appeal`

§§ `24(9) -- the Fund's financial year`

-- s 24(9): "The financial year of the Fund begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the financial year containing the month began in` IS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `year` ELSE `year` MINUS 1
